# Comments and class intent

Prefer **self-explanatory names and structure** over narrating obvious code.

## Language

- Write **all new or changed comments** in **English**.
- **Exceptions**: string literals, user-visible messages, protocol quotations, and identifiers required by an external API.

## When to comment

- **Do** comment non-obvious logic, invariants, algorithm/performance tradeoffs, and easy-to-misread edge cases.
- **Don’t** restate what the code already says.
- **Don’t** add verbose docblocks on every function unless the signature is insufficient.

## Class and struct documentation

- **Do** place a short block before each new or substantially edited `class` / `struct` stating **core purpose** in one or two sentences.

```cpp
// In-memory feature batch owned by the map window; not a GDAL dataset.
class FeatureSet {
  // ...
};
```

Apply these norms **in new or touched** translation units.
